UPDATE companies SET description='Bay Automotive Distribution Group, Inc. operates from Fremont, California, where it was founded in 2005.

The business distributes premium automotive parts, lubricants, filters, additives, and essential maintenance products. Its core service lines include wholesale automotive parts distribution, bulk motor oils and lubricants (synthetic and conventional engine oils, transmission fluids, greases), and filtration solutions covering air, oil, and fuel filters from recognized brands. The company positions itself as a bulk-rate supplier to retailers and service providers, though facility size, headcount, and annual volume figures are not disclosed.

Customers span the automotive aftermarket: spare-parts retailers, independent repair workshops, smaller distributors, and entrepreneurs launching automotive businesses. The Indonesian-language site explicitly lists "toko sparepart, bengkel kendaraan, distributor kecil" as typical buyers, confirming a channel-focused model that emphasizes large-quantity orders over retail sales.

The company states its differentiation rests on competitive wholesale pricing, consistent product availability, and a commitment to fast, professional service. It emphasizes partnerships with suppliers and quality-assurance processes to ensure distributed products meet market standards, framing long-term, mutually beneficial relationships as a core operating principle.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wholesale automotive parts distribution", "Bulk motor oils and lubricants distribution", "Filtration solutions distribution", "Premium automotive components distribution"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Automotive retail", "Automotive service and repair"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Competitive wholesale pricing", "Consistent product availability", "Fast and professional service", "Trusted supplier relationships", "Quality-assurance processes"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2005 -> db", "Headquarters Fremont, CA -> db", "Distributes automotive parts, lubricants, filters, additives, maintenance products -> /", "Wholesale distribution model -> /", "Services: wholesale parts, bulk oils/lubricants, filtration solutions -> /", "Customers: retailers, service providers, workshops, small distributors -> /about", "Competitive wholesale pricing, consistent availability, fast service -> /about", "Trusted suppliers, quality standards -> /about", "Address 44869 Industrial Dr, Fremont, CA 94538 -> /", "Responds within 24 hours -> /", "Languages English and Indonesian -> /about", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We specialize in distributing premium automotive parts, lubricants, filters, additives, and essential maintenance products.", "founded_year": "2005", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": ["English", "Indonesian"], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/bayautomotivedistributiongroupinc./"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bay-automotive-distribution-group-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The company describes its mission as a legacy of returning to nature, creating custom live-edge furniture and handcrafted woodwork for homes and commercial spaces.

The shop provides full-service custom design, build, and installation of wood and epoxy pieces. Its capabilities include live-edge dining tables, conference tables, epoxy river tables, kitchen and bar countertops, floating shelves, fireplace mantels, charcuterie boards, and commercial wood features. The team works with quality hardwoods, epoxy finishes, and reclaimed wood inventory, and also runs hands-on DIY epoxy and woodworking workshops where participants leave with a finished piece.

Bear Naked Wood serves residential and commercial clients, including homeowners, restaurants, offices, and retail spaces. Customers are involved from slab selection through finish choices, and the company handles both one-off centerpiece tables and larger custom installations.

The company emphasizes real wood, real craftsmanship, and no shortcuts, positioning each piece as a lasting investment built from nature and made to last for generations.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom design", "Custom build", "Professional installation", "Live-edge furniture fabrication", "Epoxy river table fabrication", "Custom millwork", "Commercial wood feature fabrication", "Residential woodwork", "DIY epoxy workshops", "DIY woodworking workshops", "Slab selection assistance", "Finish selection assistance", "Charcuterie board making", "Floating shelf fabrication", "Fireplace mantel fabrication", "Conference table fabrication", "Kitchen countertop fabrication", "Bar countertop fabrication"], "industries": ["Residential", "Restaurant", "Office", "Retail", "Commercial"], "materials": ["Hardwoods", "Epoxy", "Reclaimed wood", "Live-edge wood slabs"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["2,000-square-foot showroom for in-person slab selection", "Full-service custom design, build, and installation", "Hands-on DIY epoxy and woodworking workshops", "Customer involvement in wood species, finish, and detail choices", "Focus on live-edge and epoxy river table craftsmanship"], "facts_used": ["Location: Fenton, Michigan -> db", "2,000-square-foot showroom -> /about-us", "Custom design, build, and installation services -> /", "Products: live edge dining tables, epoxy river tables, conference tables, countertops, shelves, mantels, charcuterie boards, commercial wood features -> /", "Materials: quality hardwoods, epoxy finishes, reclaimed wood -> /", "DIY epoxy and woodworking workshops -> /", "Industries served: homeowners, restaurants, offices, retail spaces, businesses -> /", "Customer involvement in slab, wood species, finish selection -> /about-us", "Philosophy: real wood, real craftsmanship, no shortcuts -> /about-us", "Business hours and appointment recommendation -> /", "Contact: 9149 Center Road, Fenton, MI 48430, phone , email  -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "At Bear Naked Wood, we specialize in custom design, build, and installation services that bring natural wood craftsmanship into homes, businesses, and gathering spaces.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bear-naked-wood' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Bear Wood Company operates from Charleston, West Virginia, with additional galleries in Hurricane and Morgantown. Founded in 2014 by Matt Snyder, the small woodworking business began with a mission to preserve Appalachian history by transforming reclaimed lumber into heirloom-quality furniture and decor. The company remains independently owned and employs a team of ten craftspeople.

Every piece is sawn, sanded, and finished by hand using rag-applied oils and waxes; no particle board, MDF, or laminate enters the shop.

Primary markets include direct-to-consumer home furnishings, gift retail, and wholesale distribution to independent storefronts. The product line extends to collegiate and high-school memorabilia, seasonal decor, and personalized items. Wholesale buyers can stock Bear Wood products through a dedicated inquiry channel.

The company differentiates itself by documenting the provenance of each timber source—such as floorboards from the Meadow River Lumber Company, once the world''s largest sawmill—and passing those stories to the buyer. The "Always Home" brand promise underscores a commitment to warmth, craftsmanship, and West Virginia heritage.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture fabrication", "Handcrafted home decor production", "Reclaimed wood sourcing and milling", "Hand sanding and finishing", "Personalized engraving and customization", "Wholesale order fulfillment", "Retail gallery operations"], "industries": ["Home furnishings", "Gift and specialty retail", "Interior design trade", "Wholesale distribution", "Collegiate merchandise", "High school memorabilia"], "materials": ["Reclaimed barn wood", "Reclaimed gymnasium flooring", "Reclaimed urban timber", "Meadow River Lumber Company floorboards", "Locally sourced salvaged lumber"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Handcrafted from reclaimed wood with documented provenance", "No particle board, MDF, or laminate used", "Hand-finished with rag-applied oils and waxes", "Each piece stamped with the Bear Wood Company seal", "Wholesale program for independent retailers"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2014 -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Charleston, West Virginia -> db", "Small woodworking business -> /about-us", "Handcrafted furniture from reclaimed wood -> /", "Team of 10 employees listed -> /about-us", "Three gallery locations in Hurricane, Charleston, Morgantown -> /", "Wholesale program for retailers -> /", "No particle board, MDF, or laminate used -> /about-us", "Hand-finished with oil, wax, rag-applied finishes -> /about-us", "Rustic States collection made from reclaimed wood with documented history -> /about-us", "Materials sourced from local barns, businesses, homes, bowling alleys, gymnasiums -> /about-us", "Meadow River Lumber Company floorboards used -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We''re a small woodworking business nestled in West Virginia, dedicated to preserving history and telling local stories through reclaimed wood. Every piece we create is handcrafted with care. No particle board, MDF, or laminate here\u2014just real wood, salvaged from people like you who recognize the value in reusing something good.", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "10", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bear-wood-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Bedford Weaving Mills Inc. operates its headquarters and weaving plant in Bedford, Virginia. The company is an independent, privately held manufacturer of broad loom fabrics. No founding year or founders are disclosed in public sources.

The mill specializes in broad loom weaving, producing fabrics from fiberglass, acetate, nylon, and polyester. These materials serve a range of end uses: fiberglass for industrial and commercial applications, acetate for apparel and commercial uses, nylon for industrial and aerospace programs, and polyester for apparel and industrial markets. The facility runs a quality system certified to ISO 9001:2000.

Customers span industrial, commercial, apparel, and aerospace sectors. Specific examples include nylon fabrics supplied for aerospace applications and fiberglass fabrics used in commercial and industrial settings.

The business emphasizes its independence and ISO-certified quality management as foundations for consistent fabric production. No further differentiators or origin story are provided in available materials.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2000']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Broad loom weaving"], "industries": ["Industrial", "Commercial", "Apparel", "Aerospace"], "materials": ["Fiberglass", "Acetate", "Nylon", "Polyester"], "equipment": ["Broad looms"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Independent, privately held ownership", "ISO 9001:2000 certified quality management", "Broad loom weaving across fiberglass, acetate, nylon, and polyester", "Fabrics supplied to aerospace, industrial, apparel, and commercial markets"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters and plant in Bedford, Virginia -> db", "Independent, privately held manufacturer -> /", "ISO 9001:2000 certified -> /", "Weaves fiberglass fabrics for industrial and commercial applications -> /", "Weaves acetate fabrics for apparel and commercial applications -> /", "Weaves nylon fabrics for industrial applications and aerospace -> /", "Weaves polyester fabrics for apparel and industrial applications -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Bedford Weaving Inc. is an independent, privately held manufacturer of high-quality broad loom fabrics.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bedford-weaving-mills-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Beeken Parsons was established in 1983 by Vermont furniture makers Bruce Beeken and Jeff Parsons in the Farm Barn at Shelburne Farms, a 1,400-acre working farm and National Historic Landmark in Shelburne, Vermont. The studio began as a collaboration between the two craftsmen, focusing on custom furniture made to order.

The company designs and fabricates custom furniture, integrating design, craftsmanship, and wood sourced from local forests. Operating as a furniture studio on the grounds of Shelburne Farms, Beeken Parsons produces pieces for both residential household clients and contract professionals.

The client base spans residential customers and contract professionals furnishing institutional settings such as libraries, schools, religious buildings, and civic auditoriums. The studio works directly with clients to develop pieces suited to each environment.

Beeken Parsons states that its process begins with careful listening and communication, integrating design and craftsmanship with the finest local woods. The founders describe their approach as paying deep attention to the art of making furniture beautifully, a philosophy that has guided the studio since its inception.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design", "Custom furniture fabrication", "Woodworking"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Contract furniture", "Library furniture", "Educational furniture", "Religious furniture", "Civic furniture"], "materials": ["Wood (local forests)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom furniture made to order", "Design and craftsmanship integrated with client communication", "Wood sourced from local forests", "Studio located at historic Shelburne Farms"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1983 -> /about", "Founders: Bruce Beeken and Jeff Parsons -> /about", "Location: Shelburne, Vermont -> /about, db", "Studio at Farm Barn, Shelburne Farms -> /about", "Custom furniture made to order -> /about", "Serves residential and contract clients -> /about", "Client settings: libraries, schools, religious buildings, civic auditoriums -> /about", "Wood sourced from local forests -> /about", "Process emphasizes careful listening and communication -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Vermont furniture makers Bruce Beeken and Jeff Parsons design and craft custom furniture to order.", "founded_year": "1983", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='beeken-parsons-vermont-furniture-craftsmen' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Behl Designs operates from Wellesley, Massachusetts, where founder Priyanka Behl established the studio after a career in the textile industry. Raised in India amid vibrant textiles and artisan traditions, Behl began with scarf design before expanding into custom home furnishings. The business remains closely tied to its Indian roots, with Behl traveling regularly to oversee production alongside local artisans.

The studio creates custom textiles and finished products — including hand-beaded window coverings, hand-embroidered furniture, pillows, and shower curtains — using techniques such as weaving, embroidery, and printing. Behl Designs also provides workroom services and collaborates with artists and artisans to produce their designs, offering textile swatches and yardage to interior designers. Production is carried out by skilled artisans in India under Behl’s direct supervision.

Clients include interior designers seeking swatches and custom yardage, artists and artisans looking for production partners, and homeowners purchasing exclusive items from the studio’s own line. The company serves the interior design, home furnishings, and artisan collaboration sectors.

Behl Designs was born from Behl’s lifelong fascination with global cultures, colors, and craftsmanship. She cites her upbringing in India, years in Hong Kong, and extensive travels as ongoing sources of inspiration, and emphasizes hands-on collaboration with artisans to develop unique patterns and textiles.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Workroom services", "Custom textile design", "Hand beading", "Hand embroidery", "Weaving", "Printing", "Production collaboration with artisans", "Textile swatch program", "Textile by-the-yard sales", "Custom pillow fabrication", "Custom shower curtain fabrication", "Custom window covering fabrication", "Custom furniture upholstery"], "industries": ["Interior design", "Home furnishings", "Artisan collaboration", "Textile industry"], "materials": ["Silk", "Textiles"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Direct oversight of artisan production in India", "Custom textile design and development with hand-beading, embroidery, weaving, and printing", "Textile swatch program and by-the-yard sales for interior designers", "Collaboration model for producing artists\u2019 and artisans\u2019 designs", "Workroom services for custom soft goods"], "facts_used": ["Location: Wellesley, Massachusetts -> db", "Founder: Priyanka Behl -> /about", "Background: grew up in India, worked in textile industry, started with scarves -> /about", "Works with artisans in India, travels to oversee production -> /about", "Offers custom textiles, hand beading, embroidery, weaving, printing -> /about", "Products: pillows, shower curtains, window coverings, furniture -> /about", "Services: workroom services, collaboration for production, textile swatches, textiles by the yard -> /about, db", "Target customers: interior designers, artists/artisans, homeowners -> /about", "By appointment only -> /about", "Inspiration from India, Hong Kong, travels -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "custom textiles designed by Behl and made by skilled artisans", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='behl-designs' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Bella Furniture, operating under the Marbella Designs name, is a family-owned furniture manufacturer based in Bell Gardens, California, in the greater Los Angeles area. The company describes itself as having decades of experience in the art of upholstered furniture, though a specific founding year is not disclosed.

The shop produces custom upholstery including tailored sofas, sectionals, pillows, and custom seating for hospitality and commercial spaces. Each piece is designed and built by hand, combining traditional craftsmanship with a modern point of view. The company offers flexibility in scale, fabric, and design, working closely with clients to bring their vision to life. No facility size or headcount figures are published.

The company states that its work reflects a commitment to quality materials and responsible production, with every piece proudly made in California. It values craftsmanship, honesty in materials, and creating furniture that feels as good as it looks, positioning itself as a maker of lasting, comfortable pieces.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom upholstery", "Furniture manufacturing", "Pillow manufacturing", "Hospitality seating", "Commercial seating", "Hand-built fabrication", "Design collaboration", "Fabric selection"], "industries": ["Hospitality", "Commercial"], "materials": ["Fabric", "Upholstery materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated", "Hand-built custom upholstery", "Made in California", "Flexible customization in scale, fabric, and design", "Specializes in hospitality and commercial seating"], "facts_used": ["Location: Bell Gardens, California -> db", "Family-owned -> /", "Custom upholstery, furniture, pillows -> /", "Hospitality and commercial seating -> /", "Hand-built, made in California -> /", "Decades of experience -> /", "Flexibility in scale, fabric, design -> /", "Commitment to quality materials and responsible production -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a family owned furniture company dedicated to the art of upholstered furniture. Every piece we create is thoughtfully designed and carefully built by hand", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bella-furniture-marbella-designs' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Bellona USA operates from Las Vegas, Nevada, as a distributor and retailer of Turkish-manufactured furniture. The company does not disclose its founding year, ownership structure, or founder names on its public-facing materials.

The business curates modern and luxury furniture collections — among them Boheems, Valenty, Picasso, Veronica, Montella, Estella, Plaza, and Mona — spanning living room, dining room, bedroom, and accent categories. It maintains a physical showroom with a virtual tour, runs a dealer portal that provides access to a Basic Line Catalog and an Exclusive 2025 Catalog, and coordinates consumer financing through Synchrony with an 18-month 0% APR offer. Orders over $5,000 qualify for free shipping.

Bellona serves both retail consumers and wholesale buyers.

